exports[`getContract coerce (the boundary clamps) given: a TREE-SHAPED dobj that must reference itself when: it self-references DIRECTLY, mid-initializer then: it fails with a message that names z.lazy as the fix 1`] = `
"✋ ConstraintError: Reply.contract() requires a static schema. either declare \`static schema\` (zod) on Reply to use .contract() — or, if this call is a SELF-REFERENCE from inside Reply's own \`static schema\` initializer (a tree-shaped dobj), the field is not assigned yet at that moment: defer it with \`z.lazy(() => Reply.contract())\`

{
  "domainObject": "Reply"
}"
`;

