exports[`getContract coerce (the boundary clamps) given: a dobj whose constructor rejects what its schema accepts when: the payload reaches the constructor through a PARENT contract then: c10 — the message names the dobj AND the next move 1`] = `"Wave.contract(): the props satisfied the schema, but \`Wave.build(props)\` threw — a wave over 100ft is not rideable. fix: align \`static schema\` with what the constructor demands (e.g. its \`static nested\` hydration), so any payload the schema accepts can also construct"`;

exports[`getContract coerce (the boundary clamps) given: a dobj whose nested hydration fails when: the contract parses a payload the hydrator rejects then: c11 — the hydration error text survives, un-flattened 1`] = `
"Rig.contract(): the props satisfied the schema, but \`Rig.build(props)\` threw — ✋ NestedDomainObjectHydrationError: DomainObject property Rig.hardware was declared as a nested domain object with 2 options and had a ._dobj key specified on the input. However, the specified ._dobj was not found as one of the declared nested domain object options. In other words, the correct class constructor was not present on the DomainObject.nested definition.

Please check the declared nested domain object options for Rig.hardware and update it to include Skeg, or correct the ._dobj value in the data to match a declared option.

{
  "key": "hardware",
  "prop": {
    "_dobj": "Skeg",
    "count": 3
  },
  "declaredNestedClassNameOptionsForProp": [
    "Fin",
    "Leash"
  ]
}. fix: align \`static schema\` with what the constructor demands (e.g. its \`static nested\` hydration), so any payload the schema accepts can also construct"
`;

